WEBVTT

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:04.620
Yukiho...?

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.290
You go to Nubilum.

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:15.410
Yes, Ma'am.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.000
Yukiho!

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:24.450
Wait, Yukiho!

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:31.660
Imber...?

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.620
I'm back, Imber.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:39.290
Haruka!

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.290
Haruka!

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.660
Yukiho...

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.540
Haruka...

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.790
Haruka!

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:18.500
Underneath this sky, I have always

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.910
Continued to search for my dream

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.500
All alone...

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:30.120
Where does everyone go forth for their journey?

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.660
The days in my memories grow distant

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:40.410
Your smile from back then supports my heart now

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:47.160
Your smile from back then supports my heart now

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:57.500
I'm sure that with our silent profiles, both you and I

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:01.040
Understood that these personas exist

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.620
Because of our injuries

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:08.290
We say we do this for happiness or for love

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:12.750
As we repeat this cruel battle

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:16.370
Yet even so, the tears won't stop

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:20.790
Our hopeful hearts are one

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:27.540
Our own futures are calling to us

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.750
Goodbye

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:38.250
So then, was she able to secure Imber?

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:42.500
Yes, however it would appear Mondenkind
has figured out what we are doing.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:44.950
Have the soldiers hurry.

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:45.750
Sir.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:50.410
Squadrons Delta and Echo
have secured L2.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:54.790
Squadron Charlie is now heliborne.
They have begun heading toward Point 3.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:57.450
Squadron Alpha is
advancing toward Point 1.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:00.370
Just two left...

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.910
Prometheus 1 and 2 still aren't responding.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.500
Obstruction fading has
deteriorated to Level B.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:10.120
I can individually discern
Prometheus 1 and 2 now.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.120
I have pinpointed their locations!

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:14.700
What's that?

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:18.580
Prometheus 1, 2 and 3.
I cannot identify the other craft,

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.790
but looking at the numbers
for its gravitational waves...

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:22.790
Is it Hiems?

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:26.250
No way! They've finished
putting it together already?!

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:29.290
Prometheus 1's
identification code just changed?

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:34.450
The new passenger is... Chihaya Kisaragi?

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:40.080
We're picking something up at Point C3,
E7! Its identification code is unknown.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.580
I believe it's with the Turiavita!

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:45.080
I've verified the identification signal
at Point S5, T7.

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.700
Isn't this... the MSA?!
It's Headquarters' assault force.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.200
I did it again...

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:17.620
I... I let you get hurt.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:20.950
And here I have someone waiting for me.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:22.950
I...!

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:28.080
Is that me?

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:31.790
You've been watching me?

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:36.660
Will you move for me?

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:38.290
Nebula!

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:44.120
You're right. This isn't like me.

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:47.660
I can't give up. There's no way
I'm going to give up!

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:52.370
C'mon. Let's go, Nebula.
You'll be okay, won't you?

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:56.450
After all, you've got me here with you!

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.620
Let's go, Nebula!
Idiot Ribbon is waiting for me!

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:10.120
Up?!

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:14.500
Sorry for the wait!

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.000
What's this? You can still move?

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:21.830
That darn Makoto went
easy on you, didn't she?

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.950
Then I'll be nice and play with you a bit.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.160
I've confirmed that Nebula has restarted!

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:32.410
System interference...? His
communications function isn't responding.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:35.870
Turiavita have fanned out with their
iDOL units as their central force.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.120
They are currently engaged
in combat with the MSA units.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:42.290
Have the MSA prioritize securing the iDOLs
and request that they avoid confrontation.

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:45.330
A moment, please! We have received
a notice from Geneva.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:49.160
MSA has positioned a special
command unit at Port Moresby.

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:53.160
Henceforth, the iDOL Team
will fall under that unit's command.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:57.370
Does that mean they want us
to sit quietly and watch?

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:01.500
This is quite the mess. Dang.

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.910
We must avoid repeating
the tragedy that happened...

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:07.870
...at the Dawn of the Purple Moon.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.330
Haruka...!

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:18.450
Yukiho, we're taking that girl with us.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:19.290
Okay.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:24.330
Why...?

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.620
Why are you doing this?!

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:32.620
Yukiho, aren't you Haruka's friend?!

00:06:33.160 --> 00:06:35.120
You entered Mondenkind together...

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.290
Didn't you two work hard together?!

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:40.750
I did it for Chihaya.

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:45.040
I merely did that so Chihaya
could take Imber back.

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:46.580
How could you...?

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:51.790
Getting close to her, letting her ride Imber,
cheering her along...

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:53.330
It was all...

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:55.330
...for Chihaya!

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:59.040
It's what Chihaya wanted.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:03.290
I'm done talking to you.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.620
There is a new signal
coming from Point D4!

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:22.200
What?! Is it another enemy?

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:23.450
No, it's not.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:26.330
There's gravitational distortion?

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:28.950
Anything from the command unit?

00:07:29.080 --> 00:07:30.330
Nothing!

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:38.910
That's-!

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:40.290
What?!

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:49.750
It can't be!

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:00.790
No way...

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.410
It's the fifth...

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:07.580
...iDOL.

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:17.410
Tempestas!

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:21.500
Now of all times...

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:24.660
We've lost three and
now the fifth shows up.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:27.250
This is definitely bad.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:34.330
Th-this is Command Platoon No. 3! An
iDOL of unknown affiliation has appeared.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.450
Give us our orders!

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.750
Wh-what? What is that?

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:18.290
Tempestas...

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.580
What's that sound?

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:38.790
Wh-what's that?

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:54.580
You're halfway decent!

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:55.870
Shut up!

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:07.660
Wh-what is it? Nebula?

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:09.910
Nebula, what's the matter?

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.080
Nebula has shut down!

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:15.410
It appears Imber, Nubilum and Hiems
have also shut down.

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:17.790
What is going on?

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:21.370
Why...? He isn't reacting.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:33.160
That's...

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:42.580
Hiems?

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:47.000
What's that sound?

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:53.870
This is...

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:02.750
This sound... It's the same from back then?

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:39.200
Look!

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:41.700
It's Konpeito Snow.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:43.370
Was that in the weather report?

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.580
The gravity fluctuations are abnormal.

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:49.200
Both the Honey Belt and Sugar Belt
are greatly deviating from their orbits.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.200
Does this mean it's calling out?

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:56.450
Aulyn is?

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:59.000
That is the natural way to
interpret the phenomenon.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:01.000
In which case, we truly must...

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.370
We have no choice but to use THAT
to keep it at bay.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:06.750
You mean... Vulturius?

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:10.700
But we will be sacrificing
five hundred million in one blow.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:12.250
The numbers are irrelevant.

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:16.500
What matters is that we prevent
the birds from leaving their cage.

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:32.620
Imber...

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:39.620
My head...!

00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:42.040
Mama!

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:51.290
Nebula, what's gotten into you? Tell me!

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:54.750
The various Prometheus units
are still down.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.250
Haven't we heard word
from the Command Unit yet?!

00:12:57.620 --> 00:12:59.250
We're still under orders to stay on standby.

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:01.620
Access to lines: All clear.

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:05.250
No abnormalities in
Main Energy V-01, V-02 and V-03.

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:08.040
All sections, please enter Stage 2 Standby.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:11.700
It would seem we're all set.
Requesting permission to activate.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:13.370
Granted.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:15.080
Granted.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:16.620
Granted.

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:21.330
The codes are in consensus.
I am activating Vulturius.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:26.160
Sugar Belt is unaffected by
the abnormal gravitational pull.

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:29.410
There are magnetic abnormalities in
the stratosphere. I am looking into them.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.160
V-01: Activate.

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:33.500
Next. V-02: Activate.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.910
V-03: Activate. Deploy the mirrors.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:05.410
Mami, are you in there? Mami!

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:11.620
Mami!

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:19.700
This aurora...

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:22.540
I must hurry.

00:14:34.950 --> 00:14:36.000
That's...!

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:41.870
Makoto...!

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:54.500
There's no mistake about it.
She's the real deal.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:58.870
This is Search Team 1.
We've secured the target.

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:08.120
A large 5km long aurora has been
observed with New Guinea at its center...

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:11.790
You can now see the homing waves
targeting all of the Prometheus units!

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:15.500
Critical emission capacity
in T minus: 186 seconds.

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:17.330
Homing waves: Fully locked on.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:20.160
Adjusting by 5.88 for
magnetic abnormalities in the air.

00:15:20.160 --> 00:15:22.160
There is a possibility of further fluctuation.

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:26.870
That's cool as long as we can destroy
all five units at once.

00:15:27.160 --> 00:15:29.700
Vulturius?! Do they truly intend to fire it?

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:34.200
I confirmed that it has been activated.
I predict it will fire in 180 seconds.

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:36.790
Anything from the Command Unit?

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:38.450
We still haven't heard anything.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:41.500
Aren't those the satellites
we launched recently?

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.290
What's going on?!

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.290
Weren't they observation satellites?

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.830
But in reality...

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:51.000
If we fire that,
a large tsunami will hit Japan!

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.330
There's no point in telling that to me...

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:59.370
Please send a request to Geneva
to execute an emergency shutdown!

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:00.620
On the double!

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:08.290
What are you trying to do?

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:12.790
Doesn't matter.
Aren't I free to do as I please?

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:15.620
It's no longer any of your business.

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:17.500
Makoto...

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.410
Aren't you the one who said
you didn't need me?!

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:26.250
That aside, tell me.
Tell me what you really are.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:27.870
What I really am?

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:29.830
I saw it.

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:32.580
I saw the mark on Chihaya Kisaragi.

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:37.250
Tell me. What the heck are you?

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:40.450
I am...

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:43.830
The sound...!

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:50.000
It's gone?

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:55.450
What?

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:57.160
The sound...

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:08.200
Isn't that...?

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:15.200
Makoto!

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:24.540
Imber... Yukiho, we're pulling back.

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.160
Yukiho?!

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:31.750
I can't! He isn't moving...

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.540
Tempestas...

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:42.450
"Run for it"?

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:45.700
Critical emission capacity
in T minus: 60 seconds.

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:47.200
All parts are normal.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.000
It's out of Geneva's jurisdiction?

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:53.450
Weren't they the highest
authority in Mondenkind?!

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:55.910
I have no idea what this is all about!

00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:58.500
It has entered the final stage for emissions.

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:01.160
Someone, anyone, stop that thing!

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:12.330
All missiles self-destructed
upon reaching maximum altitude.

00:18:12.620 --> 00:18:15.660
The target is too far away.
Normal weapons cannot reach it!

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:18.250
Ram Epimetheus into it.

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:19.370
But...

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.250
We cannot let it destroy them!

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:23.250
It is the only light...

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:24.250
Epi?

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:28.500
...leading to the mischling!

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:31.410
I've confirmed that the various
Prometheus units have reactivated.

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:34.910
Epimetheus is leaving New Guinea.
It is headed toward the satellites.

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:40.660
I hate to say it,
but I'm strict about being on time.

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:42.370
We are beginning the countdown.

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:47.540
30, 29, 28, 27,

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:48.330
What?
30, 29, 28, 27,

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:55.250
26, 25, 24, 23,

00:18:55.620 --> 00:19:00.250
22, 21, 20, 19,

00:19:00.250 --> 00:19:01.830
Tempestas!
22, 21, 20, 19,

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:07.580
18, 17, 16, 15,

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:09.540
14, 13, 12, 11,

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:10.290
Mami!
14, 13, 12, 11,

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:13.750
14, 13, 12, 11,

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:21.160
10, 9, 8, 7, 6,

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:29.080
5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0.

00:19:45.790 --> 00:19:50.950
And thus, humanity will be forever
trapped within its cage.

00:19:56.660 --> 00:19:57.580
Chihaya!

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:13.870
Vulturius has hit its target!

00:20:14.120 --> 00:20:17.830
The area hit is at latitude
five degrees south. Altitude at... 100?!

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:23.660
The altitude is at 100?

00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:34.000
Tempestas!

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:20.500
Tempestas!

00:21:56.250 --> 00:22:05.200
Like a saint that crosses the ages

00:22:05.200 --> 00:22:14.160
In what kind of loneliness did you cry?

00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:23.040
Stretching out to a star so far away

00:22:23.040 --> 00:22:31.580
Say, I'll depict my feelings, look up at the sky

00:22:33.200 --> 00:22:43.040
Dear boy, if I always look for you in my heart

00:22:43.040 --> 00:22:52.000
Ah, I'll release a light so strong it will envelop you

00:22:52.000 --> 00:23:00.950
That sparkling trail will be the guide for us both

00:23:00.950 --> 00:23:12.540
Now, no matter where we look, we feel the truth

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:41.040
Preview
The Way Back

00:23:27.120 --> 00:23:30.290
About the long-eyed scissors crab
living in New Guinea.

00:23:30.290 --> 00:23:32.750
It is of the blue crab or long-clawed family

00:23:32.750 --> 00:23:35.500
and are widely distributed
across the tropics.

00:23:35.700 --> 00:23:37.580
It's characteristic for its long eyes.

00:23:38.120 --> 00:23:41.040
About the depressed red rock crab.
Its shell has knots projecting-
